    "evidence_text": "Recorded Live On Stage\n\nRecorded Live On Stage is the name of a 1963 live album recorded by Motown star Mary Wells.\n\nLive at Luther College\n\n, which was played at the end of the song \"Jimi Thing\".\n\nIdina Menzel: Live at Radio City\n\nComatose Comes Alive\n\n The band's first live DVD was the Alien Youth DVD, which featured an acoustic performance.\n\n The album is a CD of the concert's audio and a DVD capturing the live show.\n\n However, John Cooper's speech after \"Savior\" is cut from the CD.\n\n This is also the first release to feature Jen Ledger on drums.\n\nRadio City Music Hall\n\nRadio City Music Hall is an entertainment venue located in Rockefeller Center in New York City.\n\n Nicknamed the \"Showplace of the Nation\", it was for a time the leading tourist destination in the city.\n\nLive at Radio City\n\nLive at Radio City is a live album and video by Dave Matthews and Tim Reynolds recorded at Radio City Music Hall on April 22, 2007.\n\nPete Price\n\n The show is aired live from 10pm to 2am and follows an open forum format.\n\nLive Radio City Music Hall 2003\n\n This concert would also be the last of Luther Vandross' career.\n\nJoin Together (album)\n\n Several of the tracks were recorded at Radio City Music Hall, New York, and at Universal Amphitheater, Los Angeles, with the rest from various other concerts during the tour.\n\nLive at Celebrity Hall\n\n.",
